{"toolCallId":"call_dba4325282f2411ea9fa4d547c717395","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"specFolder\": \"zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent\",\n  \"description\": \"Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\",\n  \"keywords\": [\n    \"min-percent\",\n    \"option\",\n    \"calculate-completeness\"\n  ],\n  \"lastUpdated\": \"2026-10-26T16:56:26.777Z\",\n  \"specId\": \"001\",\n  \"folderSlug\": \"completeness-min-percent\",\n  \"parentChain\": [\n=== REQ rows ===\n76:| REQ-001 | `--min-percent <N>` is accepted and consumed with its value; the script exits `3` when the completion it reports is below `N` and `0` otherwise. | Against a folder whose reported completion is `C`: `--min-percent $((C + 1))` exits `3`, `--min-percent \"$C\"` exits `0`, `--min-percent 0` exits `0`. |\n77:| REQ-002 | The report output is unchanged with and without the option, in both text and `--json` form. | On the same folder, stdout of a `--min-percent` run is byte-identical to stdout of the same run without the flag; a `diff` of the two is empty. |\n78:| REQ-003 | An invalid `N` is a usage error: non-integer, negative, above 100, or a missing value each exit `1` with a message on stderr and no report. | `--min-percent abc`, `--min-percent -1`, `--min-percent 101` and a trailing bare `--min-percent` each exit `1`; stdout carries no report. |\n84:| REQ-004 | The gate runs after the report is written, so a failing run still prints its full report before exiting `3`. | An exit-`3` run emits the same complete report as an exit-`0` run. |\n85:| REQ-005 | Without the option the script behaves exactly as before, including exiting `0` on success. | The pre-existing assertions in `calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts` pass unmodified. |\n86:| REQ-006 | `show_help` lists `--min-percent <N>` and the exit-code comment block records code `3`. | `--help` output names the option; the trailing comment block lists `3 - Completion below --min-percent`. |\n87:| REQ-007 | When `--json` and `--min-percent <N>` are passed together, the JSON output gains a boolean field `min_percent_met`, `true` when Overall Completion is at or above `N` and `false` otherwise. | On a folder reporting Overall Completion `C`: `--json --min-percent \"$C\"` emits `\"min_percent_met\": true`, `--json --min-percent $((C + 1))` emits `\"min_percent_met\": false`, and a `--json` run without the option emits no `min_percent_met` field. |\n=== new task ===\n48:- [ ] T012 Emit `min_percent_met` in the `--json` object when `--min-percent` is also passed, set from the same reported completion the exit gate uses, and add a case asserting `true`, `false` and the field's absence without the flag (REQ-007) (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`, `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts`)\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/wa3f8a76d29/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"600b1e","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
